><doc-number>7183646</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8031871-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8031871</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9102658-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9102658</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations> </citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HISHINUMA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO RYO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURITA HIDEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CHEMICALS CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HISHINUMA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, RYO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURITA, HIDEYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CHEMICALS CORP.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HISHINUMA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO RYO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURITA HIDEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HISHINUMA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, RYO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURITA, HIDEYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of producing a flexible substrate which grows a metal bump (16) by using a mask film patterned by a photolithography process. When an opening is formed in a polyimide film without using a laser beam, a fine opening can be formed accurately thus enabling a fine metal bump (16) to be formed accurately. After the metal bump (16) is formed, the mask film is removed, a liquid resin material is applied before drying to form a coat and the coat is cured to form a resin film. The tip end of the metal bump (16) can be exposed if the surface is etched during the coat forming process.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à un procédé servant à produire un substrat souple destiné à former par croissance un bossage métallique (16), en utilisant un film masque dont le motif est obtenu par un procédé photolithographique. Lorsqu'une ouverture est ménagée dans un film de polyimide sans utilisation de faisceaux laser, une fine ouverture peut être ménagée avec précision, ce qui permet de former avec précision un bossage métallique fin (16). Après la formation de ce bossage métallique (16), le film masque est enlevé, un matériau à base de résine liquide est appliqué avant le séchage pour former un revêtement, et celui-ci est durci pour former un film à base de résine. L'extrémité en pointe du bossage métallique (16) peut être exposée si la surface est attaquée pendant le processus de formation du revêtement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>